Z||000000||gtsonly||08-26-2001||07:16 AM||||I am rebuilding the heads on my car and I am to the point of buying some new internal stuff. What do you all suggest to make the car run stronger...IE: rocker arms, lifters, valve springs. Anu help would be welcomed<P>------------------<BR>Chris Hatch <BR>1986 GT w/T-TOPs||||reg||6
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||08-26-2001||10:56 AM||||Hey GTS!<BR>I would replace the springs and lifters at the least...<BR>Go to any competent machine shop and talk to the mechanic doing the work and let him know what you want, heck, he might even clean up the ports for you, if you ask nicely!<BR>Don't forget though, the more you want done the more it costs...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||08-26-2001||12:06 PM||||Bring the heads up to ABT machine in Hopkington MA and ask for a performance valve job. Get the SI stainless steel valves and have the machinist undercut the valves for more low lift flow. ABT did my heads and did an excellent job. I think it was only $200 too. If you are keeping the stock camshaft than you don't need to replace the stock springs with performance valve springs although you can. Stiffer springs will only increase the potential reline of your engine and with the stock camshaft you won’t gain much. I would get new stock springs as well as new GM lifters. The Crane Magnum roller tip rockers are your best bet if you want to replace the rocker arms.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
